# Build-time public configuration for the web app.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* belongs here — everything in this file is compiled into
# the client bundle and is world-readable. Never put a secret here.
#
# NODE_ENV is deliberately absent: `next build` sets it to production itself,
# and injecting NODE_ENV=development from the shared .env silently broke the
# build for weeks with a misleading "<Html> should not be imported" error.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is deliberately EMPTY.
#
# The deployment serves the web app and the API from one origin: vercel.json
# rewrites /api/v1/* to the API serverless function. An empty value makes the
# client use relative URLs, which is what keeps it same-origin — and lets the
# session cookie stay SameSite=Lax instead of needing SameSite=None.
#
# It must NOT be set to localhost here. NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time,
# so a value in this file is compiled into the public bundle; the previous
# localhost:4000 default is exactly why the first deployment called the
# visitor's own machine. Local development gets its value from the root .env
# instead, which `next dev` loads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
